WEBVTT

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:17.370
No way!

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.370
Mana-chan, go around to the left.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.480
Got it!

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:25.750
Satoka!

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:26.920
I'll attack!

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:30.460
Yuumi!

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:32.760
Go!

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:37.840
Oh, no!

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:46.980
Sato-chin, are you okay?

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.230
Yes, but it doesn't look like we'll 
be able to stop him that easily.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.860
Io-san, take it from here.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.240
You won't get away!

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:01.870
Io-chin!

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.000
Tsubame-san!

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.060
Tsubame-chan!

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:12.960
Watch out, Tsubame!

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:27.000
<b>Deploy! Fifth Force</b>

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.150
I can't believe it got away again.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.220
We came so close, too.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.120
Well, no use in getting too down about it.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.540
This is our third failure, though.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.210
That's enough to bring anyone down.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.040
Tsubame-chan!

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.840
We might have failed this time, 
but let's work hard to succeed next time.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:55.460
Anyway, let's all have some 
good food and cheer up.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.630
Yes, that's an excellent suggestion.

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:03.070
Yeah, no point in staying depressed.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:08.180
Everyone, we're going to 
be late if we don't hurry!

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:08.650
What?

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.440
Oh, no!

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.410
It's morning.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.690
We're going to be late!

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.780
<i>The newly established 
Goryoukan Academy for Girls.</i>

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:26.740
<i>It boasts a campus in the middle of 
the city and well-furnished facilities.</i>

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:30.250
<i>It has both a middle and a high school, 
and is quite popular.</i>

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:36.140
<i>And this school has one more side to it...</i>

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:39.620
Good morning.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.260
Um...

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.490
Is Yaginuma Io-san here?

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.390
Io-chin has a volleyball tournament!

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.620
Oh, that's right.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:52.790
I wish all of us could go cheer her on.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.860
Congratulations on your win!

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.770
Thank you.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:07.250
We heard that you received an offer 
to train as an Olympic athlete.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.790
Yes, I suppose that's true.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.770
Will you be appearing 
in any commercials soon?

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.540
I, uh...

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.040
Sorry, could you look this way?

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.260
Over here, too!

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.780
This part is important,

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.970
so make sure you remember it.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:27.180
Okay, well, that's it for today.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.140
Oh, Sajima Yuumi-san.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:34.400
Yes?

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.900
Could you come to the staff room later?

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.960
So, what is this about?

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.040
Hero Odagiri Yukako!

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.330
This is the sword of legend, Excalibur!

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:55.330
Since you've managed to pull it out,

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:59.590
you are qualified to become 
the legendary King Arthur!

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:01.360
Sajima-san.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.050
Yes?

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:08.790
I'm asking why that was stuck 
in the ground in the backyard.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.980
Oh, dear! You figured that out, too?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.300
It's the mysterious holy sword that 
lies dormant in the backyard!

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.060
What?

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:20.500
Do you think this could become one 
of the seven wonders of this school?

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:26.180
We're a new school, so we don't 
have anything like that, you know?

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:26.740
That's why—

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.600
That's why you were trying to 
fabricate a school mystery?

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.510
O-O-Of course not!

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:35.220
"Fabricate" makes it sound like a crime!

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:40.940
I was just trying to liven up the rather 
sterile environment of this school.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:46.200
And then someone'd find it and be like, 
"Wow, I found this really cool sword!"

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.400
Anyway, that thing is dangerous, 
so I'm going to have to confiscate it.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.980
What?!

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:56.780
Or not.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:59.770
Here. I'm sorry.

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.780
Maybe I was being too obvious…

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.060
What's the matter, Yuumi?

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.830
Oh, Ryouko-chan.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.260
Did you do something again?

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:21.230
"Again"? Don't make it sound like 
I'm always doing something bad.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.840
Sorry about that.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.840
It's true, though.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:32.320
I never imagined Yukako-sensei 
would be the legendary King Arthur.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:35.850
I don't quite know what you're talking about...

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.270
The seven mysteries of the school, huh?

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:46.370
Our school doesn't really have 
anything mysterious about it, right?

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.910
Do we really need that?

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.930
A school without its seven mysteries

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:56.410
could easily get a talking-to 
from the Board of Education.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:02.090
Y-Your views on education 
are pretty biased, I see.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:06.130
But I do understand how Yukako-sensei feels.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.130
Huh?

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.930
Hey, hey, hey.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:11.800
What is it?

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:17.170
They've been really active lately.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:18.710
Really?

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.660
We have to work hard, Yuumi.

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:22.920
Yeah.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:25.070
I'll work hard on the seven mysteries, too.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.730
Huh? You're not giving up on that?

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.100
Of course not.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:33.900
It's my job to bring fun 
and joy to the school!

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:43.250
I wonder why Yuumi-chin got 
called to the staff office.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.040
Who knows?

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:45.850
Huh?

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:49.920
Sato-chin, didn't you have 
curry bread for lunch, too?

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:51.640
This is a snack.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:55.220
It serves a different purpose than lunch.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:56.220
Oh?

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.580
Sounds kinda complicated, but okay.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:01.650
Phew. That was tiring.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:03.190
Heya, Yuumi-chin!

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.600
What are you two doing here?

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:09.640
I'm here because Io-chin will be 
back soon. And Sato-chin is...

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:10.700
Eating a snack.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.990
I heard she won her volleyball match!

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.470
Huh? Really?

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:19.440
Then let's all surprise her 
at the school gate.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:22.190
To get Io-san in a surprise attack 
as she comes back...

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:23.790
It's to congratulate her!

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.520
Tough luck.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:32.690
Io-chin, welcome back!

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.460
Congrats on your win!

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.510
Congratulations.

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.030
Thanks.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:39.910
It was just a district tournament, though.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:42.850
We'll all go to cheer you on 
when you reach the nationals.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.600
Yeah, thanks.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.580
Can you go home yet?

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:49.430
The team takes the day 
off after tournaments.

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:50.940
Yay!

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.760
You're that happy?

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.730
Well, since you're so popular,

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:57.530
we never get to go home with you.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.120
Yeah, sure.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:03.380
I hope Tsubame-chin can come to school soon.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:04.360
Yeah.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:05.940
Oh, right...

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.380
I want to stop by somewhere first.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:12.170
Let's see...

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.320
Scary school stories.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.470
Mysteries based on true stories.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.220
The school's seven mysteries, huh?

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.260
That sounds like fun!

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:23.710
I know, right?

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.980
But Yukako-sensei found out about it,

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.900
and I got in trouble.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:31.190
I know one story.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:34.910
A ghost with long hair?!

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.030
Yes.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:42.030
In a hallway in the school, 
when the sun is almost down,

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.750
a lone girl with long hair...

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:48.130
That's enough, Satoka.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:50.840
I was curious, so I did a little investigating.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.850
Surprisingly, there were a
lot of people who saw her.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:58.860
I kind of want to see that ghost-chin!

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:01.390
Don't use "-chin" for ghosts.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:05.350
The school when the sun 
is almost down, huh?

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:08.090
Y-You couldn't...

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:14.330
A-Are we really going to look for this ghost?

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:18.440
Putting aside whether or not we 
can use it for our first mystery,

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:21.290
in any event, we need to 
determine the story's validity.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:25.410
I was also of the opinion that 
we couldn't just discard it.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:29.080
I'm not good with stuff like this.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.740
I hope she'll show up soon.

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:33.150
This is so exciting!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.670
Did you hear that?

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.390
Is that...

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.260
...footsteps?

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:45.890
Yeah...

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:55.780
It...

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:57.890
It couldn't be...

00:09:58.530 --> 00:09:59.950
She really...

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:02.410
...appeared?

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:06.490
Huh?

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.250
What are all of you doing here?

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.670
Tsubame-chan!

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.670
Tsubame!

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.670
Tsubame-chin!

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.670
Tsubame-san!

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.190
Me? A ghost?

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.880
Yes.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:35.460
Most likely, the students that 
saw you mistook you for one.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:39.440
I thought my heart was going 
to stop for a second there.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:40.990
I'm sorry about that.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.790
No, it's okay.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:45.870
But why were you at the school by yourself?

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.760
Sometimes I go when everyone's gone.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:53.340
I just kind of wondered what 
the school you all go to is like.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.970
I see.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.580
So you're not a ghost-chin, then.

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:59.500
I guess it's not very good to do that, huh?

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:00.840
I'm not even a student.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:05.780
You're going to go to school 
with all of us eventually, right?

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:07.890
Yeah. It's important to get a look.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:10.390
She's right, Tsubame-san.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.140
Yes, you're right.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:18.820
Fifth Force.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:21.780
Everyone, please assemble.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.740
Sorry we're late!

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:29.450
Altair Torte is here.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:32.670
Now everyone is here.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:34.660
Please look at this.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:39.180
In the past few days,

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:42.970
the frequency of distortions in the 
border has been increasing, moshu.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:47.800
So that's why the O'bli have been 
appearing in the border more often.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.430
We just have to wipe all of them out.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:55.400
We're going to need stronger patrols.

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:58.720
It's going to get even busier than before,

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:00.710
so be aware of that.

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:01.920
Tierra-sensei.

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:04.610
It'll be fine.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:08.270
Just leave it to Procyon Pudding.

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:10.920
What are you doing speaking out of turn?

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:12.250
I'm the leader.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:13.800
Right, whatever.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:16.200
What? You got a problem?

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:19.760
Oh, my. You two are really close.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.880
How do you figure?!

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:25.720
I expect even more out of you, Fifth Force.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:26.970
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:41.090
<i>The O'bli: inter-dimensional distortions 
in time-space that are invading us.</i>

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.070
<i>To repel the O'bli, we have the Strikers.</i>

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:46.900
<i>In other words, girls with the ability</i>

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:51.620
<i>to detect the fifth dimension and take out
the O'bli are called the Fifth Force.</i>

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:04.610
<i>And the unknown objective 
of Goryoukan Academy</i>

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:09.870
<i>is to find individuals for the 
Fifth Force and train them.</i>

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:13.030
<i>The Time-Space Administrator, Tierra,</i>

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:16.500
<i>scouts students that show potential</i>

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.260
<i>and chooses them for the Fifth Force.</i>

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:23.380
<i>That is, with one exception.</i>

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:42.520
Researching the O'bli, moshu?

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:43.880
Yeah.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.470
This is the most I can do 
while everyone's at school.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:53.810
Some of them are in the form 
of humans, while others are not.

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:56.740
There are many types.

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:59.560
And there are many that haven't 
been confirmed yet, moshu.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:04.390
Moshune-chan, what are the O'bli after?

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:06.650
What type of damage will they cause?

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:11.970
The only thing we know in this world is 
that they come from the fifth dimension,

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:15.290
and that normal humans 
cannot detect them, moshu.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.730
In this world...

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:23.640
The worlds parallel to this one 
may know more, moshu.

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:27.800
But we only have fragments 
of information, moshu.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:33.510
So basically, we don't know very much at all.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:37.730
I wonder where I came from...

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:43.960
We won't know until your 
memory returns, moshu.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:45.420
Yeah.

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:51.360
You're right.

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:54.380
I won't get anywhere by feeling disheartened.

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:57.660
I see.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:02.820
So the ghost was Miyama-san, huh?

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.320
They found out about my holy sword, too.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.170
I have to think of new mysteries.

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:09.760
Hmm...

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.700
Oh, but...

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:17.270
Doesn't Altair Torte have the patrol tonight?

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.850
Oh, yeah.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:24.140
I'm sure Tsubame-chan will
be all ready and waiting.

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:26.150
She's very diligent.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:27.750
Yeah!

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:31.150
That's one of the great things about her.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:33.410
Hmm...

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:37.180
That's probably why she 
still can't come to school.

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:39.050
Huh? What?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:44.710
I was just thinking it would suck if 
we ran into anything on our patrol.

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:51.700
It hasn't been long since 
your team was established.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.340
You can run away if you need to.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:55.680
We can't do that.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:00.730
We have to save this world.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:04.560
That's why I joined the Fifth Force.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:06.150
I think

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:11.310
you have the talent to be a Striker.

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.360
Really? You think so?

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.160
You're good at cooking

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.320
and other surprising things like that.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:25.310
So you might be a surprisingly good Striker, too.

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:29.000
That "surprisingly" part kind of bugs me, but...

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:33.380
I'll do my best to get better than you guys!

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:36.300
Yeah. That's the spirit.

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:42.680
Altair Torte will be in charge 
of the patrol of Sector F.

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:44.540
Sector F?

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:47.630
That's where the O'bli 
got away from us, right?

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:52.030
That O'bli should have been taken 
care of by Procyon Pudding...

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:56.800
There's a signature around there that's strange.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:01.120
It's not a rare event for a O'bli to 
appear in the same spot twice.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.910
Huh? Really?

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:07.470
So let's all be on guard.

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:08.710
Right!

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:15.380
Here I go!

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:23.600
Yeah!

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:27.730
All right!

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:31.360
Come.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:04.200
Altair Torte is ready to go.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:04.900
Right.

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:07.100
Then I will transport you to Sector F, moshu.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:50.830
I'll never get used to coming 
to this parallel world.

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:51.950
Me, either.

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:56.400
Yeah, it looks like what we always see, but...

00:18:56.400 --> 00:19:01.070
But without anyone around, 
it feels like it's all deserted.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:06.830
Relax a little.

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:11.370
If the leader is that nervous,
everyone else will pick up on it.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:14.180
Sorry.

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:15.900
Let's relax.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:17.010
Okay.

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:24.220
A distortion in time-space.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:30.140
An O'bli!

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:31.980
It's bigger than...

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:32.650
...the last one!

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:36.270
This is Altair Torte. We have an O'bli here.

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:38.800
Confirmed, moshu.

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:40.360
It's a mid-sized Magire O'bli.

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:42.780
I'm searching for its type, moshu.

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:48.240
It seems to have greater attack power 
and speed than the last one.

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:50.180
Please be careful.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:50.960
Right!

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:52.750
You won't get away this time!

00:19:59.150 --> 00:19:59.710
Tsubame!

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:00.510
Right!

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:09.430
We did it!

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:12.640
This is bad, moshu!

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:13.480
You're not done yet!

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:17.440
We didn't take it out?

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:18.820
Run, everyone!

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:23.400
Mana-san!

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.330
Got it!

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:31.370
Get back!

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:36.880
Ryouko-chan!

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:38.380
Sorry for the wait!

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.730
Mari, finish it off!

00:20:58.930 --> 00:20:59.860
Here you go.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.860
Okay, mission complete.

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:24.640
I guess our sector didn't have anything in it.

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:28.430
It's surprising that they hit 
the same location twice.

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:30.100
Okay, let's head back.

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:33.310
Coconut Vega...

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:35.800
They're amazing.

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:42.000
I guess the veterans really are pretty good.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.820
We can't compare at all.

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:48.900
But we didn't let it get away today.

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:52.380
Yeah. That's quite the improvement.

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:53.580
Right, Tsubame?

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:58.960
Yeah.

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:01.370
You're right.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Train! And Our First Victory</b>

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:40.980
"Train! And Our First Victory."
